==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|ἔκζεμα|tr=ekzema|lang=grc}}, from {{term|ἐκ|tr=ek||out of, forth from|lang=grc}} + {{term|ζέμα|tr=zema||that which is boiled, decoction|lang=grc}}, from {{term|ζέω|tr=zeo||to boil, to seethe|lang=grc}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈɛɡzɪmə/, /ˈɛksɪmə/, /ˈɛksmə/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|eczemata|pl2=eczemas}}

# An acute or chronic [[inflammation]] of the [[skin]], characterized by redness, itching, and the outbreak of oozing [[vesicular]] [[lesion]]s which become encrusted and scaly. It is noncontagious.

====Hypernyms====
* [[dermatitis]]

====Derived terms====
* [[eczematic]]
* [[eczematous]]

